<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clades Lolliana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Lollian disaster</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The clades Lolliana was a Roman defeat in 16 BCE, when the Sugambri, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usipetes">Usipetes</a> and Tencteri crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and routed the legate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-lollius">Marcus Lollius</a>, capturing the eagle of the Fifth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a>. Though limited in scale, the disgrace brought Augustus to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and led to the campaigns of Drusus in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germania">Germania</a> from 12 BCE.</p></div>
